A recent review comparing Si, SiC and GaN likewise emphasizes application-specific power-electronic devices, thermal issues and reliability rather than a universal material ranking.<ref name="widegap">''Power Electronics Revolutionized: A Comprehensive Analysis of Emerging Wide and Ultrawide Bandgap Devices'', ''Micromachines'' 14(11), 2045 (2023), [https://doi.org/10.3390/mi14112045 DOI:10.3390/mi14112045]. Review rather than an original device measurement.</ref>

A '''larger band gap is not a universal measure of superiority'''. Material choice is a multi-criteria engineering decision involving field strength, mobility, thermal transport, wavelength, reliability, growth defects, integration, available process technology, cost and end-use conditions.

== Fabrication, measurement and system interfaces ==

A semiconductor material becomes a functioning device through engineered composition, geometry, interfaces and contacts. Depending on the process, manufacturing involves single-crystal growth and wafer preparation, thin-film deposition, lithography, etching, diffusion or ion implantation, annealing, dielectric growth, metallization, testing, dicing and packaging. These processes have occupational, chemical and resource requirements; they are not interchangeable across all materials or technology nodes.<ref name="osha">US Occupational Safety and Health Administration, [https://www.osha.gov/semiconductors/silicon/device-fabrication ''Semiconductors — Device Fabrication''], silicon processing steps and associated hazards.</ref>

Device characterization can include current–voltage curves, capacitance–voltage measurements, Hall measurements, optical spectra, temperature-dependent measurements, microscopy and defect analysis. An electrical measurement constrains a model only when contact behavior, geometry, calibration and operating conditions are specified.

At system scale the chain is '''material → device → circuit → component → system'''. The semiconductor is essential to many processors, sensors, memories and power converters, but it does not itself define an algorithm, programming language, microarchitecture or firmware. See [[Electric current/Technical|Electric current]], [[Voltage/Technical|Voltage]], [[Resistor/Technical|Resistor]], [[Computation/Technical|Computation]] and [[Computer architecture/Technical|Computer architecture]].

== Model selection and unresolved engineering limits ==

* '''Equilibrium vs driven operation:''' one Fermi level is appropriate at thermal equilibrium; driven carrier populations may require separate quasi-Fermi levels.
* '''Nondegenerate vs degenerate:''' the Boltzmann formulas and conventional Einstein relation are not universal at high carrier density.
* '''Bulk vs interface:''' trapping, surface recombination, Schottky barriers, band offsets and oxide charge can dominate a device despite good bulk material.
* '''Diffusive vs ballistic:''' drift–diffusion is a continuum model; short transport lengths, high electric fields and quantum confinement can require nonlocal or quantum transport.
* '''Electrical vs system merit:''' faster or smaller individual devices do not guarantee a faster or more efficient system without interconnect, memory, thermal, yield, power-delivery, software and workload considerations.
* '''Verification vs explanation:''' a citation supports a particular scientific premise or historical account; experimental device performance still requires actual measurements under stated conditions.

